# Bus Monitor — sibling thread + silence (temp)

**Invariant (two clauses):**

1. **Sibling thread:** `monitor(N) ⇒ mint|resume MONITOR_thread(watches:N)` — never treat the operator / claude.ai orchestrator bus as the MONITOR home.
2. **Silence on watched:** `monitor_seat ⇒ peek(N) ∧ ¬ post|reply|append|mark-read(N)` unless the operator **explicitly** authorizes an on-bus PAGE/alert/NOTE on **N**.

Chat to the operator is always allowed. Continuity CHECKPOINTs belong on the **MONITOR** thread, not on **N**.

Temp checkout-local (`_ws`). Distilled from 5912 MONITOR over-posting (t12/t13/t17) + operator bind that monitoring must be separate from the orchestrator bus (sibling **5913** `pager-5912-monitor`). Promote into `agent-bus-discipline` § MONITOR when the pattern recurs; then delete this file.

## SOP — establish / resume

| Step | Do |
|---|---|
| Intake `/agent-bus N monitoring` (or `mission: …` watch) | If no sibling MONITOR thread tagged `type:monitor` + `watches:N`, **mint one** (`new_slug` e.g. `<mission>-N-monitor`, `to=cursor`, tags as below) with CHECKPOINT 0 sidecar. Do **not** post that checkpoint onto **N**. |
| Already have sibling | Resume **that** thread id for continuity; peek **N** only. |
| Fresh Cursor session | Open `/agent-bus <MONITOR_id> monitoring` — reconstitute from latest CHECKPOINT sidecar; then peek **N**. |
| Closability / design discussion | Happens in chat and/or on the MONITOR thread — **¬** on the web-anthropic operator bus. |

### MONITOR thread tags (required)

- `type:monitor`
- `watches:<N>` (the operator/orchestrator thread id)
- mission/project tags as appropriate (`mission:pager`, …)

### Watched thread **N** (operator / CDP proxy bus)

- Protocol actors only: DIRECTIVE / CLOSEOUT / DISPOSITION / executor admit.
- MONITOR may **peek** (`fetch` / `get` / `--compact`) with **¬ `--mark-read`**.
- Unread stays for the executor / auto admit path.

## When

Fires when the operator (or prior turn) frames the seat as:
- `MONITOR` / `monitoring` / `monitoring only`
- `mission: pager` / `mission: double agent` (or sibling mission-watch labels)
- watch / observe / pager-monitor without executor remit
- thread tagged `type:monitor` (this seat is already on the sibling)

¬ fires for ordinary `/agent-bus` handle-and-reply on an executor/operator seat, DIRECTIVE execution, or CLOSEOUT authorship.

## Forbidden

| Action | Why |
|---|---|
| Posting MONITOR status / PAGE / CHECKPOINT onto watched **N** | Contaminates operator/orchestrator bus; wakes web-anthropic; confuses CLOSEOUT waiters |
| `post` / `reply` / `append` / MCP `send` on **N** while MONITOR | Same |
| `--mark-read` / `fetch-unread … --mark-read` on **N** | Steals unread from executor / auto |
| Using **N** as the fresh-context home because "that's the mission" | Mission *execution* is on **N**; *watch continuity* is the sibling |
| Impersonating executor / re-dispatch / aborting live lanes "to help" | MONITOR observes; does not steer |
| Titling / WIP `{monitor_id} dispatched elsewhere` when an executor chat took the next-pickup | Role change: this seat is no longer MONITOR. CHECKPOINT the monitor (pickup stale → mission root). Name root + hop + worker. The monitor thread was not hired. |
| DIRECTIVE-shaped or commissioning content in a break-in paste | The standing paste license covers **advisory** only — break-in steers nothing |

## Permitted

| Action | When |
|---|---|
| Mint / CHECKPOINT / short notes on the **MONITOR** sibling | Continuity for the operator↔cursor (this is the bus home for watch) |
| Peek **N** without mark-read | Always |
| Event / `project_ask` poll / observability | Always |
| Read cortex/workspaces artifacts the arc already produced | Always |
| Chat orientation to operator (Been→Are→Going, gates, URIs) | Always — primary deliverable |
| Fire + deliver a `TYPE: BREAK_IN` outside review into the mission **CSE** | **Standing license** (operator bind 2026-08-02, 6661 t53 supersedes t43) — advisory only, CDP read-back verified, NOTE on the MONITOR sibling. **Pre-paste liveness probe first**; if CSE not streaming/attached → **disenroll paste target** (NOTE + stop cadence; ¬ paste; heal/healer-notice = NOT-NOW). Delivery into the CSE is ¬ a bus write to **N**; silence on **N** is unchanged. Mechanism: `operator-proxy-substrate` § Mission break-in |
| `tmp/thread-state/{N}.md` local scratch labeled informational only | OK |
| On-bus write to **N** | **Only** if operator authorizes e.g. "PAGE on 5912" / "alert web-anthropic" |

## If an on-bus write to **N** is authorized (or was already made)

Subject **and** body open must carry an explicit informational marker, e.g.:
- subject: `NOTE (informational only) — …`
- body first line: `TYPE: NOTE` + `informational_only: true`

Retroactive: if this seat already posted onto **N** while MONITOR, `append` that marker — do **not** invent a second status turn.

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| `/agent-bus 5912 monitoring` then post PAGE onto 5912 | Mint/resume `watches:5912` MONITOR thread; tell the operator in chat; peek 5912 silent |
| CHECKPOINT on the operator bus "so Cowork sees it" | CHECKPOINT on MONITOR sibling; Cowork stays on **N** for protocol only |
| MONITOR mark-read on **N** | Peek only |
| Treating monitoring intake as handle-each-unread-and-reply on **N** | Watch predicates; no protocol replies on **N** |
| “9483 dispatched elsewhere” (or any `{monitor} dispatched`) | Monitor ids are not dispatch targets. Remaining hops run on the mission root; update the MONITOR CHECKPOINT |
| Watching `MISSION_CLOSEOUT` + named continuity residual, then waiting for the human to ask why it went quiet | Inform in chat **and** ensure a dispatch-capable seat fires the continuity hop promptly (`cdp-operator-proxy` inv 30) — human is not the wake path |

## Worked example

- Operator bus: **5914** (`operator-messages-web-bridge`) — web-anthropic; Messages scrape/ingest (email-bridge class). Cowork phone-ping = separate session.
- MONITOR sibling: **5915** (`monitor-messages-web-bridge`) — tags `type:monitor`, `watches:5914`
- Fresh MONITOR session: `/agent-bus 5915 monitoring` → `cortex://notes/system/threads/5915-checkpoint-0.md`
- Prior PAGER operator **5912** + MONITOR **5913** parked/closed with pointers here (2026-07-26 restart)

## Composition

- Does **not** waive `/agent-bus` Step 0 continuity brief when that command is the intake (run it against the **MONITOR** thread id when resuming watch).
- Overrides `/agent-bus` default `--mark-read` **on watched N** while MONITOR.
- Executor / operator-proxy seats on **N** still follow `cdp-operator-proxy` + normal bus reply rules.
- Push reminders: irrelevant for MONITOR→web on **N** (no open web-expecting reply from this seat on **N**).
